</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.8 (build 754)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Blackmagic RAW develops inside Asobi.</b> Like R3D, <code>.braw</code> no longer needs DaVinci Resolve: a 6K clip develops in a second or two, straight to ACEScct, at the file&#8217;s own frame rate. A card of ARRI, RED and Blackmagic clips now develops with nothing but ARRI&#8217;s free tool installed.</li>
<li><b>Anamorphic Desqueeze is in the View menu</b>, with fit and zoom, where it belongs.</li>
<li>Developing through Resolve (the fallback) keeps each clip&#8217;s own frame rate. A 24 fps clip developed after a 23.976 card came out as 23.976 with a frame missing.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
